# Expected results of copy.cas, written by hand from docs/design/mtp.md
# 7.8. Format: ../README.md. At every point of every row: the existing
# file's contents are under its own name or under a backup name reported;
# a copy reported done has its data under the target name; a copy failed
# after its data was complete keeps it under a reported temporary path or
# is reported failed with the temporary file deleted, never done.

CPY-001
  row a: done; C:\Dest\a.jpg holds the 1,000 bytes; no ~MTP file left
  rows b, d, e, f, g, j, k: failed (k: cancelled); the temporary file deleted; no a.jpg; nothing else reported
  row c: ~MTP0001.TMP used; done
  row h: the temporary file kept and its exact path reported; not done
  row i: as row h (the temporary kept; its path reported)
  never the target touched before size check, flush and close have all succeeded
end

CPY-002
  row a: done; a.jpg holds N; the backup deleted; no ~MTP file left
  row b: failed; a.jpg holds O; the temporary deleted; nothing changed
  row c: ~MTP0001.OLD used; done
  row d: a.jpg holds O again (moved back); the error reported; the temporary deleted
  row e: done; the backup's exact path reported (it stays)
  row f: both stay: "Your original file is now <backup path>; the copied file is <temporary path>." with both exact paths
  row g: a.jpg holds O; the error reported; the temporary's path reported
end

CPY-003
  row a: copied (at the ceiling)
  rows b, c: refused before the copy, with the size shown
  row d: refused or failed by free space (FAT16: no per-file rule); the original untouched
  row e: not refused in advance; a write failing mid-copy fails the copy by step 2
  row f: copied; the sizes past 2^31 written with SetFilePointer's high part
end
